 "review": [
  {
   "title": "MSX overview: Arabic and English differ (nothing corrected)",
   "items": [
    "Founding date: Arabic gives 21 June 1988; English gives only “June 1988”.",
    "Company form: English says “closed joint-stock company (MSX)” in 2021; Arabic says شركة مسقط للبورصة (ش.م.ع.ع), an abbreviation that normally means a public joint-stock company.",
    "The year 2021 appears only in English. The Arabic phrase ضمن تطوير قطاع أسواق المال (as part of developing the capital markets sector) has no English counterpart.",
    "English adds “(bonds and stocks)” after “securities and equities”; Arabic has only الأوراق المالية والأسهم.",
    "Trading hours: English adds “Official” and “daily”.",
    "MSX30: Arabic calls it the main measure of movement of “active stocks” (الأسهم النشطة); English says it tracks “the top 30 most liquid stocks” and links to an external site. Headings differ: مؤشرات السوق (plural) vs “Main Indicator”.",
    "Price monitoring: Arabic says smart app or official website; English says official MSX app only.",
    "Heading: تأسيس السوق (establishment of the market) vs “Market History”."
   ]
  },
